{"term":"hare","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b022c1ec41c97cfbdb","definition":"Any of several plant-eating mammals of the genus Lepus, similar to a rabbit, but larger and with longer ears.","example":"The hare has a reputation for exciting desire. Hare soup is credited with a particular aphrodisiac value.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a88660d4bba4b8799a","definition":"The meat from this animal.","example":"Ashe bit absent-mindedly into a piece of hare and swore mildly when he burned his tongue.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:740aee89b1d691a0c4","definition":"The player in a paperchase, or hare and hounds game, who leaves a trail of paper to be followed.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d50b345cbad19e0c1f","definition":"To move swiftly.","example":"But Wales somehow snaffled possession for fly-half Jones to send half-back partner Mike Phillips haring away with Stoddart in support.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["rabbit","race","speed","tear"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hare#Engl